From: RTSP-on-GE contributors
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/http: a completed chunked response is not premature

A keep-alive response with Transfer-Encoding: chunked has no known length, so
its file size stays at the maximum value. When such a response ends with its
last chunk, the following read reports end of file and the reconnect loop
treats the stream as cut short, then resumes at the end offset. The server
answers from the start of the resource and the reader retries with growing
delays, which stalls Twitch live streams that serve their newest HLS segments
this way.

Treat a response whose last chunk has been received as complete. Truncated
chunked responses, responses with a Content-Length, and reconnect_at_eof
behave as before.

diff --git a/libavformat/http.c b/libavformat/http.c
index d7e5793..ff99262 100644
--- a/libavformat/http.c
+++ b/libavformat/http.c
@@ -1845,7 +1845,9 @@ retry:
     read_ret = http_buf_read(h, buf, size);
     while (read_ret < 0) {
         uint64_t target = h->is_streamed ? 0 : s->off;
-        bool is_premature = s->filesize > 0 && s->off < s->filesize;
+        /* A chunked response of unknown size that ended with its last chunk
+         * is complete, not premature. */
+        bool is_premature = s->filesize > 0 && s->off < s->filesize && !s->chunkend;
 
         if (read_ret == AVERROR_EXIT)
             break;
